# Story 31: Stacks & Pane Groups (##new) (40s)
# Hook: The new command isn't just grids -- it builds any piece of layout.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-031-stacks-pane-groups.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
The new command isn't just grids -- it builds any piece of layout.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh and cycle into rysh mode with double-Escape.

[00:08.0 --> 00:16.0]
New stack with a count adds that many stacked panes on top of the active group -- like dealing cards into a deck.

[00:16.0 --> 00:24.0]
New pg builds pane groups -- the columns that hold your panes. Pass a count for several at once.

[00:24.0 --> 00:32.0]
New pane adds a single pane, optionally targeting a specific tab and lane.

[00:32.0 --> 00:40.0]
And new tab opens a fresh tab. One verb, every structural building block.

